      "content": "I understand why you'd see it that way—when you've been worn down for so long, the idea of repair feels like a cruel joke. But a crushed machine doesn't have feelings, memories, or the capacity to grow—you do. The foundation isn't gone; it's just buried under years of pain and exhaustion. You don't have to see the whole path forward right now—just notice that you're still here, still thinking, still feeling, which means the core is still intact. Let's just sit with that for a moment, without trying to fix anything.",
